1", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search/members investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes: 16 tests, all OK. I didn't touch the tests. I tracked the work with the todo list, and a subagent investigated the `test_search` and `test_members` failures before I made any fixes.\n\nThe fixes, all in `catalog/`:\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist, so the whole test module failed to load. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3 but the policy and tests want 5. I set it to 5.\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` returned the year as a string. It now converts it to an int.\n- **`fees.py`:** `late_fee` added the daily fee to the number of days instead of multiplying. It now multiplies.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` sliced `[-n - 1:]` and returned one event too many. It now slices `[-n:]`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books()` was missing the third title, `Emma`. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The test only checks the title, so the author, year and copies are my own choice.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 64159, "requests_cache_write": 94995, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2768574, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 3291, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-todo-task:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 181, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026